ew-phase: planning","rebar-version: 0.13.1 (ca6810a4816)","regver: aa61189569d34126","verified-at-sha:ca6810a4816bc8efc5bd41521250492166cba37c","dep 54e2ba76702666582b591897b9a71bbc0f59ffed7e46f2fbc07802255b4cc05f src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py","dep cb420ce321fa3a0e78d83c9662bd436b66ac1a3fe40bf12ea5e09c3181a26813 src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py","dep absent tests/scripts/reducer/test_inbound_relationship_scan.py","read-set: 7","read-path: src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","read-path: src/rebar/_ids.py","read-path: src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_selection.py","read-path: src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py","read-path: src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py","read-path: src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","read-path: src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py","currency-basis: file_impact"],"material_fingerprint":"fd294cc2b3d7d80d","merged_log_commit":"ca6810a4816bc8efc5bd41521250492166cba37c","principal":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","signature":null,"signed_at":1793324550784615000}},"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":13},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"573f6515f7f55071d5624c8cd7e484f99a54c41022a0b953940d25d93eba2e4a","event_uuid":"8a069cf2-a1f4-4583-b63c-e46bd10957b5","position":{"commit_sha":"e4ce03178c9f62e04f2e82878c13055737b2c740","position":"1793329186841863391-8a069cf2-a1f4-4583-b63c-e46bd10957b5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced on a store copy at origin/main ca6810a4: one inbound scan for d70a-97d9 opens 141,085 files, 609.5 MB. Confirmed by reading _replay.py that only CREATE/EDIT/LINK/UNLINK/SNAPSHOT change parent_id or deps (REVERT acts only on ARCHIVED). Plan refined: exclude -PRECONDITIONS-SNAPSHOT.json (shares the -SNAPSHOT.json suffix, never replayed), name the test module, and define the 50-ticket comparison as the old all-files candidate scan versus the new one.","timestamp":1793323851967967001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Compared on a copy of the live store (9,746 entries): 53 tickets (50 sampled at random with seed 20261029, plus the 3 most-linked LINK targets 1503-a8eb, 9594-1f1c, 8903-efb2). Old result = find_inbound_relationships with the pre-change all-files candidate scan (one shared pass, same byte-substring test); new = the restricted scan. 0 mismatches across 55 inbound links and 9 children in total. Per call: old 141,092 files, 609.6 MB; new 13,280 files, 150.9 MB. Limit of the sample: most random tickets have no inbound relationships; the fixture test covers each event type explicitly.","timestamp":1793325108556068001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on e54ff7dc706: lint, typecheck, import-convention guard green; 19,847 passed, 90 skipped, 0 failed.","timestamp":1793328911743219001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793301736491063001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"df3f181f-023a-4049-bcf9-cf45f6cb31a9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"dff5-6fe2-646c-4a0e"},{"link_uuid":"8a069cf2-a1f4-4583-b63c-e46bd10957b5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b677-5b19-c3f6-4563"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n`show_ticket` always computes `inbound_deps` by byte-scanning every event file in the store (src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py, lines 39-72). On a clone of the live store, 2026-10-29, that is 139,978 files and 609 MB read per call. Only CREATE, EDIT, LINK, UNLINK and SNAPSHOT events change deps or parent (src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py). Restricting the scan to those types read 13,258 files and 150.5 MB, and found all 15 confirmed inbound links for the 1 ticket tested.\n\nCaveats:\n- The scan trusts that the filename suffix matches the event type inside the file.\n- Link targets are stored as written, so a link stored by alias is missed by an id byte scan. That gap exists in the current scan too; on the clone, 2 of 1,605 LINK targets are not canonical ids, and both are free text.\n\nRe-checked 2026-10-29 on a fresh copy at origin/main ca6810a4: one scan for d70a-97d9 opens 141,085 files and reads 609.5 MB. In `_replay.py`'s handler table, `parent_id` is set only by CREATE and by EDIT `fields`, `deps` only by LINK/UNLINK, and SNAPSHOT restores both; REVERT acts only on ARCHIVED. Event files are written as `{timestamp}-{uuid}-{EVENT_TYPE}.json`. `-PRECONDITIONS-SNAPSHOT.json` files also end in `-SNAPSHOT.json` but are not replayed, so the suffix test excludes them.\n\n## Plan\n1. Restrict the inbound scan to files ending in `-CREATE.json`, `-EDIT.json`, `-LINK.json`, `-UNLINK.json` or `-SNAPSHOT.json`, excluding `-PRECONDITIONS-SNAPSHOT.json`, before opening them. Update the module docstring and the docstring in src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py that describes the scan.\n2. Test first (seen failing on current code): a fixture with one inbound relationship in each of CREATE (parent), EDIT (re-parent), LINK, and a SNAPSHOT-compacted ticket, all found; a COMMENT naming the target that must not make its ticket a candidate; and an open() spy asserting no other event type is opened.\n3. Compare on a copy of the live store: for 50 sampled tickets plus the 15-link ticket, compute the old result by running `find_inbound_relationships` with the old all-files candidate scan (one shared pass over the store computing every sampled id's candidates, verbatim old matching) and the new result with the new scan; require equality, and record files and bytes read per call before and after.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] The scan opens only CREATE, EDIT, LINK, UNLINK and SNAPSHOT event files; verified by the open() spy test in tests/scripts/reducer/test_inbound_relationship_scan.py.\n- [x] inbound_deps is identical to the current code for at least 50 tickets sampled from a clone of the live store; recorded in a ticket comment with the sample size and files/bytes read per call before and after.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py\n- tests/scripts/reducer/test_inbound_relationship_scan.py","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py","reason":"restrict the scan to relationship-bearing event types"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py","reason":"docstring describing the scan"},{"path":"tests/scripts/reducer/test_inbound_relationship_scan.py","reason":"per-type and open() spy tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b677-5b19-c3f6-4563"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"33ce5372-f89e-469d-bb32-236d42cd829c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0076-375d-430c-4822","ticket_type":"bug","title":"show_ticket's inbound-link scan reads every event file in the store","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e14b5a12-bc1d-4afa-895d-9749cab8cbd1","7d03eb1d-5987-4e67-8c52-08ccf2873c14","09c6b18b-381f-4c1c-b26d-d7d14628de96","9357efc8-93e1-4dbe-ab4e-da0691dc26d3","6f443e76-d845-4c22-9903-59aab8999c8e","e7231c81-90ec-4630-ab19-f13faf7166d4","b873d867-70ef-46cc-8630-79b6155dc772","